EXPLANATION = {"title": "Bond Angle", "principle": "Backbone bond angles (N-CA-C, CA-C-N, O-C-N) stay within 18 degrees RMSD of Engh-Huber ideals.", "rationale": "The pinned code (definition v2, WP-SCI-1) measures RMS angular deviation of backbone bond angles: N(i)-CA(i)-C(i) intra-residue; peptide O(i)-C(i)-N(i+1) and CA(i)-C(i)-N(i+1) across valid sequential pairs using the NEXT residue's nitrogen. Definition v1 used the same residue's nitrogen for O-C-N. WP-8: rewritten from the incorrect peptide-bond-length description to match the pinned measurement. LAW-120 is currently CONTAINED pending re-validation."}
